CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp20 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ member typedef mem-init survives: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
Resolution 2026-07-30: same mode-availability finding as
cpp20_extern_template_copy_ctor_abort -- the clang builtin
(__add_rvalue_reference) only lexes in CLANG mode; run with --stdlib
libc++ the member-typedef mem-initializer converts and the program
verifies.  The GCC-mode failure was an artifact of the reduction
harness's flags, not the libc++ bug being chased.
